abstract: >-
  HiveBlot reads Western blot figures together with their captions and methods
  text and turns each blot into lane-level evidence records. Every field in a
  record carries a status (supported, ambiguous, conflicting or missing) and
  the source wording it was drawn from; when a figure and its text disagree,
  the field is flagged as conflicting and left empty instead of guessed. The
  software combines OpenCV panel detection, a vision-language model, and
  deterministic biology and UniProt reconciliation rules, and includes a
  search API and a web interface. This is a beta release: the reviewed corpus
  covers three papers, and a pre-registered blind benchmark on unseen papers
  is in progress, so no accuracy figures are reported here.
